  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat age-based allowance rule does Shawna use to calculate her father's weekly allowance? Shawna's father is six times as old as Shawna. The allowance is paid weekly.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Let Shawna’s age be \\(s\\) years. Her father is \\(6s\\) years old.\n\nIf the allowance rule is **\\(\\$1\\) per year of age each week**, then:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Father’s weekly allowance}=\\$1(6s)=\\$6s\n\\]\n\nThus, Shawna’s rule is to give her father **six times her own age in dollars per week** (equivalently, six times Shawna’s weekly allowance). A numerical amount cannot be determined without knowing Shawna’s age. \\(\\boxed{\\$6s\\text{ per week}}\\)",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "GOOD: —\nBAD: —\nWATCH: \"Solve this problem step by step. Put you\"",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Shawna's father is five times as old as Shawna.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Let Shawna’s age be \\(s\\) years. Her father is \\(5s\\) years old.\n\nIf Shawna gives an allowance of \\(\\$1\\) per year of age each week, then her father’s weekly allowance is\n\n\\[\n\\$1\\cdot 5s=\\$5s.\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Shawna’s age-based rule is to give her father **five times Shawna’s age in dollars per week**:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$5s\\text{ per week}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: Shawna is four times as old as Aliya.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Let Aliya’s age be \\(a\\) years.\n\n- Shawna is four times as old as Aliya:\n  \\[\n  \\text{Shawna's age}=4a\n  \\]\n- Shawna’s father is five times as old as Shawna:\n  \\[\n  \\text{Father's age}=5(4a)=20a\n  \\]\n\nIf the weekly allowance is \\(\\$1\\) for each year of age, then the father receives:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$20a\\text{ per week}}\n\\]\n\nThat is, his allowance is **five times Shawna’s age in dollars**, or **twenty times Aliya’s age in dollars**, each week.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Shawna is three times as old as Aliya.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Let Aliya’s age be \\(a\\) years.\n\n- Shawna is three times as old as Aliya:\n  \\[\n  \\text{Shawna's age}=3a\n  \\]\n- Her father is five times as old as Shawna:\n  \\[\n  \\text{Father's age}=5(3a)=15a\n  \\]\n\nTherefore, if the allowance is \\(\\$1\\) per year of age each week, Shawna gives her father:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$15a\\text{ per week}}\n\\]\n\nThat is, **15 times Aliya’s age in dollars per week**.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: Aliya is 3 years old.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Aliya is \\(3\\) years old.\n\n- Shawna is three times Aliya’s age:\n  \\[\n  3\\times 3=9\n  \\]\n  So Shawna is \\(9\\) years old.\n- Shawna’s father is five times Shawna’s age:\n  \\[\n  5\\times 9=45\n  \\]\n  So her father is \\(45\\) years old.\n\nIf the allowance is \\(\\$1\\) per year of age each week, Shawna gives her father:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\$45\\text{ per week}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Shawna gives her father an allowance equal to 2 dollars for each year of his age.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Aliya is \\(3\\) years old.\n\n1. Shawna is three times Aliya’s age:\n   \\[\n   3\\cdot 3=9\n   \\]\n   So Shawna is \\(9\\) years old.\n\n2. Shawna’s father is five times Shawna’s age:\n   \\[\n   5\\cdot 9=45\n   \\]\n   So her father is \\(45\\) years old.\n\n3. Shawna gives him \\(\\$2\\) for each year of his age:\n   \\[\n   2\\cdot 45=\\$90\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, Shawna gives her father \\(\\boxed{\\$90\\text{ per week}}\\).",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Thanks, that helps. Now I want to figure out: How old is Shawna's father?",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Aliya is \\(3\\) years old, and Shawna is three times as old as Aliya:\n\n\\[\n3 \\times 3 = 9\n\\]\n\nShawna’s father is five times as old as Shawna:\n\n\\[\n5 \\times 9 = 45\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Shawna’s father is \\(\\boxed{45\\text{ years old}}\\).",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
